      "id": 1,
      "text": "Leesville was founded in 1874, originally called Leesburg, and later renamed Leesville by the U.S. government.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leesville%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 1830s, Henry O'Neill’s family settled on the east bank of Castleman's Creek, later O'Neill Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/leesville-tx",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early industry included a brick kiln and a factory that made saddletrees and stirrups.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/leesville-tx",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Leesville’s historic core sits along FM 1682, where the original church and cemetery still host local events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
